> As far as I know, you'd need to look for the "#ifdef WIN32" bits in the
> openvpn source - so, no formal documentation outside the source.

http://git.infradead.org/users/dwmw2/openconnect.git/blob/HEAD:/tun-win32.c=
 has it mostly in one place.=20

At about line 201 the example above shows how you configure the driver
with the Legacy IP addresses using TAP_IOCTL_CONFIG_TUN. In an ideal
world of course the driver shouldn't care about those, but since Windows
networking is kind of brain-dead and we have to emulate an Ethernet
device, the driver needs to know them so it can fake ARP for Legacy IP.

For IPv6 you need to ensure that the link-local address of the router on
the TAP interface is configured as fe80::8, since the TAP driver handles
ND for that address only. See=20
http://git.infradead.org/users/dwmw2/vpnc-scripts.git/blob/HEAD:/vpnc-scrip=
t-win.js#l166


